------------------------------
create-cartesian-mesh-and-GEQDSK.sh
------------------------------
Runs `tds-gs/run_3_taylor.sh` to generate the `interpolated.gf` and 
`my_new.mesh` files needed as inputs for `2d-cartesian-mesh.cpp`. 

Once those are generated, it automatically executes:
- `2d-cartesian-mesh.cpp`
- `GEQDSK-generation.cpp`

Final output: a ready-to-export `GEQDSK.txt` file.

------------------------------
README Folder
------------------------------
Contains:
- PowerPoint presentations detailing the internship work
- `Required_Variables_for_EFTI_Writer.xlsx` — a spreadsheet documenting the 
  variables used for the GEQDSK writer

Reference:  
https://freeqdsk.readthedocs.io/en/stable/geqdsk.html

------------------------------
2d-cartesian-mesh.cpp
------------------------------
Interpolates a given `.mesh` file into a Cartesian mesh and visualizes it 
with the corresponding `.gf` solution.

Outputs:
- `interpolated.gf`
- `my_new.mesh`

Note: If run independently, make sure `tds-gs/run_3_taylor.sh` (or equivalent) 
has been executed to generate required input files.

------------------------------
GEQDSK-generation.cpp
------------------------------
Creates the final `GEQDSK/GEQDSK.txt` plasma file by:
- Extracting values from individual `GEQDSK_[variable_name]` files
- Generating additional required variables
- Appending everything into the final GEQDSK file

See `README/Required_Variables_for_EFTI_Writer.xlsx` for parameter descriptions.

------------------------------
GEQDSK Folder
------------------------------
Contains:
- `GEQDSK.txt` — the final export-ready GEQDSK file
- `GEQDSK_[variable_name]` files — individual parameter files generated 
  by `GEQDSK-generation.cpp`

------------------------------
Contours Folder
------------------------------
- `contour_line_XXXXXXXX.txt`: Contains (r, z) coordinates for contours at 
  specific ψ values.
- `all_contours_radial_points.txt`: Contains (r, z) coordinates of all contours, 
  aligned radially from the plasma boundary to the magnetic axis.

------------------------------
Contours_Plot Folder
------------------------------
- `plot_contours_and_radial_points.py`: 
   Given `all_contours_radial_points.txt` and several 
   `contour_line_XXXXXXXX.txt` files, it plots:
   - Radial points
   - Corresponding contour lines
